  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Brazilian Justice and Peace Commission</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Brazilian Justice and Peace Comission (CBJP) aims at strengthening and integrating the work of the different Justice and Peace Groups throughout the country and advocating for issues such as electoral corruption, peace culture and the protection of social rights. 

This project is part of the Economic Justice Programme, a partnership between CAFOD and 4 church-based organisations, whose goal is to achieve greater economic justice in Brazil by addressing the key development issues of debt, trade, governance and human rights with a focus on awareness-raising, participation, social mobilisation and advocacy.

The project is: (1) publicizing the Economic Justice Programme&apos;s theme &quot;debt, social rights and social security system reform&quot; in the dioceses; (2) training 200 pastoral and social agents on the issue of social rights; (3) encouraging the creation of new Justice and Peace Groups in the dioceses; (4) strengthening the partnership between the Church in Brazil and other church-based organisations.</narrative>
  </description>
